      "viewText": "Example\nTwo phrases you will hear\n\nお願いします (onegaishimasu) is used when making a request. ありがとうございます (arigatou gozaimasu) is used when thanking staff. Both are standard polite forms.\n\nExplain\nWhy register matters\n\nStandard polite forms are the safe default in a shop. Casual forms belong with friends, not with staff you have not met.\n\nPractice\nSay it with romaji visible\n\nRepeat お願いします with romaji visible. Then cover the romaji and repeat once more; the romaji is a scaffold, not evidence of reading.\n\nCheck v1\nproduction\nYour answer\n\nThe question and any choices are shown above; this field records",
